Vercel checks for a static output directory after the build, even for a project
that is nothing but serverless functions. This directory exists to satisfy that
check and is deliberately empty otherwise.

Do not add files here. Vercel serves the filesystem before it applies rewrites,
so anything in this directory would shadow the API route of the same path — an
index.html would take over `/`, and the rewrite that sends every path to the
Nest application would never see it.
